  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "In 1975 Kodak engineer Steven Sasson built the first digital camera. The toaster-sized gadget, a cumbersome heavyweight of about eight pounds, was hardly portable, let alone handheld. Its first rudimentary picture held 10,000 black-and-white pixels. Recording it on a cassette took 23 seconds, and a playback unit showed it on a television."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        410.96141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Kodak's revenues showed its dependence on film, the profitable pillar of its business. Technical staffers were appreciative of the camera, but it needed no film. By Sasson's recollection, his superiors at headquarters called it cute and urged him to keep it hushed. A patent followed in 1978. Production never did."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        303.46141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        402.46141732283473
      ],
      "text": "The advent of digital photography proved disruptive. In June 2009 Kodak said it would stop making Kodachrome, its analogue film, citing lessened demand in the digital era. Kodak's manpower had reached an apex of about 145,000 in the 1980s. By 2012, layoffs since 2003 had slashed 47,000 jobs, alongside the shutdown of 13 factories and some 130 labs."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        195.96141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        294.96141732283473
      ],
      "text": "On 19 January 2012 the 131-year-old firm sought Chapter 11 protection from its creditors, sapped by pension costs and years of slowness in going digital. Citigroup, a lender, provided $950 million for its restructuring. A portfolio of 1,100 digital imaging patents fetched about $525 million from a consortium of twelve buyers, including the giants Apple and Google."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.46141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        187.46141732283473
      ],
      "text": "After 19 months of reorganisation, the once-mighty Kodak left bankruptcy in September 2013, downsized, streamlined, and refocused as a commercial printer for business clients. In November 2009 President Obama had decorated Sasson with national laurels, commending his digital camera. That medal's year also saw Kodak announce the end of Kodachrome."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1975年，柯达工程师史蒂文·萨松造出了第一台数码相机。这台烤面包机大小的小器械/小装置，是个笨重的大块头，重约八磅，很难说是便携的，更谈不上手持。它拍下的第一张粗糙的照片，只有1万个黑白像素。把照片录到盒式磁带上要花23秒，再由一台回放装置在电视上显示出来。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        429.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "柯达的收入显示出公司对胶卷的依赖，胶卷是其业务中赚钱的支柱。技术员工对这台相机颇为赞赏，但它不需要胶卷。据萨松回忆，他在总部的上司说它挺可爱，并敦促他对此秘而不宣。1978年，这台相机获得专利，生产部门却从未这样做过（跟进）。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        340.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        420.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "数码摄影的问世，结果证明是颠覆性的。2009年6月，柯达宣布将停产Kodachrome这种模拟胶卷，理由是数码时代里需求减少。柯达的员工规模曾达到约14.5万人的顶峰，那是在20世纪80年代。到2012年，自2003年以来的裁员已砍掉4.7万个岗位，同时13家工厂和约130个冲印室相继关闭。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        232.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        332.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "2012年1月19日，这家已有131年历史的公司申请《破产法》第11章保护，以免受债权人追讨，它受养老金负担和多年来转向数码的迟缓所慢慢抽空/消耗。贷款方（借出钱的人）花旗集团提供了9.5亿美元，用于其重组。由1,100项数字成像专利构成的组合以约5.25亿美元卖给一个由十二家买家组成的财团，其中包括巨头苹果和谷歌。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        143.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        223.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "经过19个月的改组，昔日强大的柯达于2013年9月走出破产，规模已缩小，业务经过精简，重新定位为商业印刷商，面向企业客户。2009年11月，奥巴马总统授予萨松国家级荣誉，来表彰他的数码相机。那枚奖章颁发的同年，柯达也宣布了Kodachrome 的终结。"
    }
  ],
